1
00:00:00,353 --> 00:00:02,023
(Sheldon:)Fancy a dip, my dear?

2
00:00:02,021 --> 00:00:03,621
(Leonard:)I do.

3
00:00:03,622 --> 00:00:05,692
(gasps)

4
00:00:05,691 --> 00:00:08,461
(Sheldon:)Wait, that purple
flag indicates

5
00:00:08,461 --> 00:00:11,291
(Sheldon:)that marine pests, such
as jellyfish, are present.

6
00:00:11,297 --> 00:00:14,367
(Amy:)Wow, that flag
is a lifesaver.

7
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:16,797
(Sheldon:)No.

8
00:00:16,802 --> 00:00:18,872
(Sheldon:)This is.

9
00:00:20,373 --> 00:00:22,443
(Sheldon:)Stop looking at my legs.

10
00:00:23,809 --> 00:00:26,139
(Sheldon:)Not a flag.
Flag.
(dinging)

11
00:00:26,145 --> 00:00:28,545
(Sheldon:)Flag.
Not a flag.

12
00:00:28,547 --> 00:00:30,147
(Sheldon:)Flag.
(buzz)

13
00:00:30,149 --> 00:00:32,749
(groans)
Crap.

14
00:00:34,153 --> 00:00:35,483
(Raj:)When stuff
like this gets me down,

15
00:00:35,488 --> 00:00:37,058
(Raj:)you know what I like to do?

16
00:00:37,056 --> 00:00:39,926
Sing "Hakuna Matata"
like an eight-year-old girl?

17
00:00:39,925 --> 00:00:41,925
(Raj:)Wrong, smarty-pants.

18
00:00:41,927 --> 00:00:45,427
It's "Everything Is Awesome"
from The Lego Movie.

19
00:00:47,099 --> 00:00:48,429
(Leonard:)Look at these notebooks.

20
00:00:48,434 --> 00:00:50,434
(Leonard:)They're full of pages and pages
of data.

21
00:00:50,436 --> 00:00:52,236
(Leonard:)He clearly spent years on this.

22
00:00:52,238 --> 00:00:55,008
Mmm. Oh, it's just columns
of random numbers. Toss it.

23
00:00:55,007 --> 00:00:57,907
(Leonard:)Well, but what if this was a
potential breakthrough for him?

